{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally and Vanessa Visit the Grand Canyon"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Natural Wonder"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Nature Around Us > Greetings From Alaska"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Articles"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the article <span class=\"italic\"><span class =\"strong\">a</span></span> before singular, countable nouns which begin with consonant sounds.</br></br>Examples:</br><ul><li><span class=\"italic\">He is a farmer.</span></li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"italic\">She doesn't own a motorcycle.</span></li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"italic\">I saw a colorful bird in Belize.</span></li></ul></br></br>You use the article <span class =\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">an</span></span> before singular, countable nouns which begin with vowel sounds.</br></br>Examples:</br><ul><li><span class=\"italic\">He is an astronaut.</span></li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Sally didn't get an invitation.</span></li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"italic\">I saw an eagle in the zoo.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Pronouncing <span class=\"italic\">a</span> and <span class=\"italic\">an</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Normally, you pronounce consonant letters with a consonant sound, and vowel letters with a vowel sound.</br></br>There are some exceptions. The rule for <span class =\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">a</span></span> or <span class =\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">an</span></span> is still the same. You just need to think about the sound, not the word. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:<br/><br/>  <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">a European city</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">EU</span> sounds like the consonant sound at the beginning of the word <span class=\"italic\">you</span>. </li> <li> <span class=\"italic\">a one-day tour</span><br/> The sound at the beginning of <span class=\"italic\">ONE</span> sounds like the consonant sound at the beginning of the word <span class=\"italic\">wonder</span>. </li> <li><span class=\"italic\">an F1 car</span><br/> The letter <span class=\"italic\">F</span> starts with a vowel sound, like in the two first letters of the word <span class=\"italic\">EF</span>fort. </li> <li><span class=\"italic\">an hour</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">H</span> is silent in this word, so it sounds like <span class=\"italic\">our</span>, which starts with a vowel sound.</li></ul>."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "corner "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place or area that is far away, on the edge "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Washington State is in the northwest corner of the United States. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le14ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you read in a pamphlet about a natural wonder."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "natural wonder "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something in nature that is very surprising, beautiful, or amazing "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Grand Canyon is a natural wonder."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le14ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to carve "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to create (something) by cutting into a surface "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The river carved the canyon."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le14ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "national "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "belonging to an entire nation or country "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Grand Canyon became a national park in 1919."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le14ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pilgrimage "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a journey to a shrine or location important to a person's beliefs"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We went on a pilgrimage to the holy city."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le14ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deepest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extending far down from the top or surface."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: At it's deepest point, the canyon is more than a mile down."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le14ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le14ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to a local library."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Research the Grand Canyon. List 5 new facts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 5 sentences that use these new facts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your sentences to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research information on the Grand Canyon."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I find new facts on the Grand Canyon."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write 5 sentences about the Grand Canyon."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read the sentences aloud."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn", "coverimg": "engenn", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": ""}, {"text": "", "id": 1, "time": "", "image": ""}, {"text": "", "id": 2, "time": "", "image": ""}]}}]}, {"id": 2, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"video_src": "engenn4le14ob04re2vid01", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": ""}, {"text": "The Grand Canyon is located in the northwest corner of the United States. It is close to the Utah and Nevada borders. It is one of the seven natural wonders of the world and an incredible place to visit!</br></br>", "id": 1, "time": "1", "image": ""}, {"text": "The canyon was created over millions of years by the water from the Colorado River. It is 277 miles long and 15 miles wide. At its deepest point, it is more than one mile from the top down to the river. Tourists have an opportunity to hike in an area, carved for 17 million years by a river.</br></br>", "id": 2, "time": "14000", "image": ""}, {"text": "In 1919, the Grand Canyon became a national park. Tourists  can learn about the history of Native Americans who lived near the canyon. Some considered the Grand Canyon a holy site, and made pilgrimages to it.", "id": 3, "time": "38000", "image": ""}]}}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Vocabulary and Grammar"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say and use words like a and an."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say and use intonation and prominence."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say where a place is."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Would you prefer to visit the rainforest or the Grand Canyon? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Is there a national park near your city or town? What are they like? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Name any place that is considered holy in your country."}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text